# ── Internal working documents — PATTERNS, not just the names above ──────────
# The named rules above cover the docs that exist TODAY. They do not cover the
# NEXT one, and this is a public repository: an internal plan that lands in
# `git status` as untracked is one `git add -A` away from being published.
# These patterns close the class. Verified against the tree when added: no
# tracked file matches any of them, so nothing legitimate is hidden.
*-PLAN.md
*-UPGRADE.md
*-roadmap.md
*-proposal.md
HANDOFF*.md
BOOT-PROMPT*.md
NOTES.md
SCRATCH*.md
PRIVATE-*.md
INTERNAL-*.md

# ── Domains folder (personal wiki data — lives outside the app repo) ──────────
# The wiki is managed separately (via the Sync tab / a private GitHub repo).
# Clone this repo to get the app; your wiki folder is pointed to by DOMAINS_PATH.
domains/*
!domains/.gitkeep
.playwright-mcp/

# ── Private maintainer notes (never published) ────────────────────────────────
# Personal enrolment / account guidance for the maintainer. Contains process
# notes tied to one individual's legal + payment details, not product docs.
docs/apple-developer-enrolment.md

# ── Batch-ingest queue (Track 3 — local, disk-persisted job state) ────────────
# Lives outside domains/ by construction (src/brain/paths.js's
# getIngestQueueDir()); this line is only a fallback for a repo-mode install
# where the user-data dir happens to be this repo root.
.ingest-queue/

# Runtime state written by the OpenRouter catalogue + on-wiki qualification
# features (v3.16.0). In REPO mode `getUserDataDir()` resolves to the app root,
# so these land here beside .curator-config.json and must be ignored for the
# same reason: they are per-machine runtime state, not source. This repo has
# shipped this exact class three times — .write-lock (v3.0.15), .DS_Store
# (v3.0.16) and the ingest queue (v3.3.0) — each time because a new runtime
# file was created next to tracked source and nothing excluded it.
.openrouter-catalogue.json
.openrouter-qualifications.json

# Per-installation machine identity (v3.17.0, working state). Same repo-mode
# reasoning as the block above — but this one matters MORE, because the whole
# point of the file is that it is UNIQUE PER INSTALL: committing it would ship
# one machine's identity to every clone, so two installs would resolve to the
# same `state/<scope>/<machine>/` path and silently overwrite each other's
# handoff via `git pull -X theirs`. That is precisely the data-loss bug this
# file exists to PREVENT (two Macs both named MacBook-Pro.local).
# This is the FIFTH instance of the class — .write-lock (v3.0.15), .DS_Store
# (v3.0.16), the ingest queue (v3.3.0), the OpenRouter sidecars (v3.16.1).
# Every time: a new runtime file appeared beside tracked source and nothing
# excluded it. If you add another runtime artefact, add it here in the same
# change, not in the release that discovers it.
.curator-install-id
# The chosen machine FOLDER NAME (v3.23.x, D10). Same file, same directory,
# same reasoning, one level worse: `.curator-install-id` leaks an id that only
# forms half the folder name, whereas this leaks the WHOLE path segment. Two
# clones sharing it write to a byte-identical `state/<scope>/<machine>/` with
# no hostname difference left to separate them. The SIXTH instance of the
# class, added in the change that introduced the file — which is what the
# paragraph above asks for.
.curator-machine-id

# Browser-driven test screenshots land in the repo ROOT, so a bare `git add -A`
# stages them into a PUBLIC repo. .playwright-mcp/ was already covered; the root
# was not. This project has shipped that class four times (.write-lock,
# .DS_Store, the ingest queue, the OpenRouter sidecars) — each time because a new
# runtime file appeared beside tracked source and nothing excluded it.
/chat-streaming-*.png
/*.screenshot.png


# Local mirror of the design-system bundle (v3.26.0). READ-ONLY REFERENCE.
# Kept out of the public repo because it is the maintainer's brand work, and
# so agents can read the system without a personal Drive path appearing in a
# committed file. The MASTER lives outside this repository — see
# docs/design-system-source.md. Never edit this copy expecting it to survive.
the_curator_design_system/

# ── Desktop packaging: build output and signing material ─────────────────────
# Added in the SAME change that created `desktop/`, which is what the
# .curator-install-id block above asks for: "If you add another runtime
# artefact, add it here in the same change, not in the release that discovers
# it." This is the SEVENTH instance of that class — and the first one where
# the artefact is not merely noise but a CREDENTIAL.
#
# Two categories, and the second is the one that matters:
#
#   1. Build output. `desktop/` has its own package.json (Electron must never
#      reach the root manifest — the auto-updater runs `npm install` on every
#      user's machine), so it grows its own node_modules and its own lockfile,
#      and electron-builder writes into desktop/dist/.
desktop/node_modules/
desktop/dist/
desktop/out/
desktop/release/
#
#   2. Apple signing and notarization material. THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC.
#      A Developer ID certificate, an App Store Connect key or an
#      app-specific password committed here is a credential leak that cannot
#      be undone by a later commit — it has to be revoked at Apple. These
#      patterns are deliberately UNANCHORED so they match at any depth,
#      including in a scratch folder someone makes while debugging a build,
#      and they are here BEFORE any signing work exists so no such file can
#      ever be produced into an unguarded tree.
#
#      Verified when added: no tracked file matches any of these patterns.
*.p12
*.pfx
*.cer
*.certSigningRequest
*.mobileprovision
*.provisionprofile
AuthKey_*.p8
.notarize.json
.env.notarize
